MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Multi-tenant Mimir (Argus's backend) requires an X-Scope-OrgID header on
every query; the metrics handler previously spoke only PROMETHEUS_AUTH=none
or =google. PROMETHEUS_HEADERS takes comma-separated Name=Value pairs and
applies them to every Prometheus request (auth modes still win the
Authorization header on conflict). Wired through ctx.credentials as
prometheus_headers, declared in the capability card, optional in the
CronJob's secret.

README gains the Argus recipe alongside the GMP one: gateway endpoint +
tenant header + the kubeletstats CPU/MEM query preset, validated live
2026-07-12 on an Argus solo cluster (evidence: tenishai/argus#52 — the
sweep reported first-try and both producers' measurements converged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
