+### Argus-managed clusters (Mimir)
+
+Validated live 2026-07-12 (kind + the [Argus](https://github.com/tenishai/argus)
+solo platform — evidence and measurement convergence in
+[tenishai/argus#52](https://github.com/tenishai/argus/issues/52)). Argus's
+Mimir is multi-tenant (every query needs an `X-Scope-OrgID` header naming the
+cluster's tenant) and pod metrics arrive via the OTel Collector's kubeletstats
+receiver under `k8s_*` names, not cAdvisor's. Two things differ from the
+defaults:
+
+1. **Endpoint + tenant header** — the Mimir gateway, plus the tenant:
+
+   ```
+   prometheus_url=http://argus-mimir-gateway.argus.svc:80/prometheus
+   prometheus_headers=X-Scope-OrgID=<cluster tenant>
+   ```
+
+2. **Queries** — kubeletstats names, pod-level with promoted `k8s_*` labels
+   (braces doubled — see design notes):
+
+   ```bash
+   kubectl -n gojira set env cronjob/gojira-sizing-agent \
+     CPU_QUERY='sum by (k8s_pod_name) (rate(k8s_pod_cpu_time{{k8s_namespace_name="{namespace}", k8s_pod_name=~"{app}-.*"}}[5m]))' \
+     MEM_QUERY='sum by (k8s_pod_name) (k8s_pod_memory_working_set{{k8s_namespace_name="{namespace}", k8s_pod_name=~"{app}-.*"}})'
+   ```
+
